}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review BLOCK identified an actual artifact-location conflict: the current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, while this repo’s surviving reports/tools/known-fine ledger live in `.joe-janitor/`. Recovery will use `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`, matching recorded file impact, and will carry a prominent RECOVERED / NOT A NATIVE RUN banner. The plan will also identify the protocol version visible in the transcript/history and split compound acceptance criteria before re-review.","timestamp":1786897562314341001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Recovery complete. Artifact: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` (671 lines), headed `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN`; it remains local-only under the repository’s established `.joe-janitor/` convention. Recovered run totals: 82 Discovery candidates; 54 Verification survivors (45 DEFECT, 9 HARDENING); 28 drops; 28 Remediation moves (21 agent-converged, 6 research-resolved, 1 no-consensus). The export preserves only RP-01 through RP-06. All six were approved: RP-02 as proposed; RP-01/RP-03/RP-04/RP-05/RP-06 with material refinements. The report includes transcript/repository/tracker/external evidence labels, exact source-tree corroboration at b0aac231, prior-decision context, approval status, rationale, recovery confidence, and explicit unrecoverable fields. RP-07–RP-28 were never presented before the transcript ended. Phase 5 was never reached; no cleanup epic/children or known-fine changes exist, and none were invented during recovery. No production code changed; `git diff --name-only` is empty.","timestamp":1786900480933448001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Local-only recovery artifact verification (2026-08-16 America/Los_Angeles):\n\nArtifact: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`\nSHA-256: `c8a382504f15c591505df56fd55d3c5a84313f3eb57c9c4dd71153c350426cd6`\n\nConcrete checks from `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar`:\n- `rtk wc -l .joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` -> `671`\n- `rtk sed -n '1,5p' ...` -> first line `# RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN`\\n- heading count query over `^### Decision [1-6] / RP-0[1-6]$|^## Phase [1-5] ` -> `11` (six decision records + five phase sections)\\n- `rtk git diff --name-only` -> empty; no production-code changes\\n\\nThe six decision records each contain an evidence record, recovered rationale, final Phase-4 verdict, approved refinement, explicit recovery confidence/uncertainty, and source-labeled transcript/repository/tracker/external evidence. The five phase sections name missing/unrecoverable outputs and historical/inferred mappings. Phase 5 records that exact-title tracker searches found no cleanup epic/children and that none were created during recovery. The report is intentionally git-excluded under the established `.joe-janitor/` convention, so this ticket comment is the durable attestation channel for those criteria.","timestamp":1786900640105112001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close-gate metadata correction: the recovery report is intentionally git-excluded and no repository or production-code file changed. The prior file_impact entry incorrectly implied a code change and caused the normal close precheck to require a rebar-ticket commit trailer. Replaced file_impact with an explicit none declaration; no --force bypass was used.","timestamp":1786901692821226001}],"created_at":1786897281080091001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"393020dd-dd57-4ba2-ac3a-902c57642f6a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10c8-9981-3877-4ed5"},{"link_uuid":"b5060d94-9ac4-4a62-9bc5-2ab323eaed71","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"},{"link_uuid":"f729a9f6-e5d1-4fc9-b8cb-93b9b6b37d99","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98"}],"description":"## Context\nThe generated artifacts from a rebar-janitor session were lost. Reconstruct the recoverable results from `~/Downloads/ChatGPT-Rebar janitor analysis-20260816-0915.md`. Decisions 1-6 require the deepest research and analysis. This is a no-code recovery: preserve evidence, distinguish transcript facts from present-day corroboration, and make uncertainty explicit.\n\nThe current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, but this repository’s historical local-only artifact convention is `.joe-janitor/`, evidenced by tracked `.joe-janitor/tools.md` and tracker record `naive-bigheaded-wildcat`. Other git-excluded files visible in one checkout are opportunistic corroboration only: the plan does not assume that `known-fine.md` or prior `report-*.md` files survive. The deterministic output is the intentionally git-excluded local artifact `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`. Its title and opening banner must say `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` so future runs cannot mistake reconstructed material for an original Phase-2 record. Report-content criteria are operator-attested because repository-snapshot verifiers intentionally cannot see local-only janitor reports; checksum and structural evidence are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory the source transcript, its structure, and any surviving repository/tracker evidence without modifying production code.\n- Identify the rebar-janitor protocol version in effect during the transcript from its content and repository history; use the current protocol as a guide, labeling inferred mappings if the historical structure differs.\n- Reconstruct the Phase 1/2 finding and verification context needed to interpret the later decisions.\n- Recover decisio